1
ORDINANCE NO. ___________
ENTITLED: “AN ORDINANCE AMENDING SECTION 12.04.010, OBSTRUCTIONS ON
STREETS,
AND SECTION 12.04.080, CONSTRUCTION AND
REPAIR–PERMITS REQUIRED–FEES–EXCEPTION, OF CHAPTER 12.04,
STREETS, SIDEWALKS AND DRIVEWAYS GENERALLY, OF TITLE 12,
STREETS, SIDEWALKS AND PUBLIC PLACES, OF THE CODE OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING.”
BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:
Section 1.  That Section 12.04.010, Obstructions on streets, of Chapter 12.04, Streets,
Sidewalks and Driveways Generally, of Title 12, Streets, Sidewalks and Public Places, of the Code
of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, is amended as follows:
12.04.010
Obstructions on streets, ALLEYS, SIDEWALKS, OR DRIVEWAYS WITHIN
THE PUBLIC RIGHT-OF-WAY DESIGNATION OF NUISANCE–
PROSECUTION AS A MISDEMEANOR.
A.
Except as otherwise provided by this code SECTION or other city ordinance
PROVISION OF THIS CODE, no person shall erect, maintain or in any way cause an obstruction
of any character in or upon any street, alley, or sidewalk within ANY PUBLIC RIGHT-OF-WAY
of  the city.
B.
A PERSON MAY OBSTRUCT A STREET, ALLEY, OR DRIVEWAY WITHIN
A PUBLIC RIGHT-OF-WAY TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY A RIGHT-OF-WAY
ENCROACHMENT PERMIT ISSUED BY THE CITY ENGINEER PURSUANT TO SECTION
12.04.080, SECTION 12.04.150, SECTION 12.04.230, OR SECTION 12.12.010 OF THIS CODE.
C.
A PERSON MAY, WITHOUT HAVING TO SECURE A RIGHT-OF-WAY
STORAGE PERMIT, FOLLOWING THE ATTAINMENT OF A RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE
PERMIT, OBSTRUCT A STREET, ALLEY, OR DRIVEWAY WITHIN A PUBLIC RIGHT-OF-
WAY FOR THE STORAGE OR PLACEMENT OF LANDSCAPING MATERIALS, SUCH AS
GRAVEL, ROCKS, DIRT, SOD, MULCH, BRICK PAVERS, WEED BARRIER FABRICS,
IRRIGATION SYSTEM COMPONENTS, LANDSCAPE LIGHTING COMPONENTS, AND
LUMBER, SUBJECT TO THE FOLLOWING TERMS AND CONDITIONS:
1.
THE PERIOD OF OBSTRUCTION SHALL NOT EXCEED SEVENTY-
TWO (72) HOURS    SEVEN (7) CONSECUTIVE DAYS;
2.
THE AREA OF OBSTRUCTION SHALL NOT EXCEED TWENTY-FIVE
(25) SQUARE FEET;
3.
THE OBSTRUCTION SHALL NOT UNDULY RESTRICT PEDESTRIAN,
VEHICULAR OR OTHER PUBLIC USE OF THE RIGHT-OF-WAY; AND
4.
EROSION CONTROL BEST MANAGEMENT PRACTICES (BMPs)
SHALL BE USED TO REDUCE POLLUTANTS WHICH MAY BE DISCHARGED
FROM LANDSCAPING MATERIALS AS A RESULT OF STORM EVENTS, SNOW
MELT, OR ANY OTHER APPLICATION OF WATER.
D.
A PERSON MAY OBSTRUCT A STREET, ALLEY, OR DRIVEWAY WITHIN
A PUBLIC RIGHT-OF-WAY FOR THE STORAGE OR PLACEMENT OF MATERIALS,
EQUIPMENT, OR OTHER TANGIBLE PERSONAL PROPERTY THEREIN  (OTHER THAN
LANDSCAPING MATERIALS) TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY A RIGHT-OF-WAY
STORAGE PERMIT ISSUED BY THE CITY ENGINEER.  FOR THE PURPOSES OF THIS
CHAPTER, THE TERMS “PERSONAL PROPERTY” AND “EQUIPMENT” SHALL INCLUDE
```

