2
STORAGE CONTAINERS AND ROLL-OFFS.
E.
THE OBSTRUCTION OF ANY STREET, ALLEY, OR DRIVEWAY WITHIN A
PUBLIC RIGHT-OF-WAY BY THE STORAGE OR PLACEMENT OF MATERIALS,
EQUIPMENT, OR OTHER TANGIBLE PERSONAL PROPERTY THEREIN WITHOUT
HAVING OBTAINED, WHEN REQUIRED, A RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE PERMIT, OR
FOLLOWING THE EXPIRATION OF SUCH A PERMIT, SHALL CONSTITUTE A NUISANCE
AND A MISDEMEANOR PUNISHABLE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE PENALTY
PROVISIONS OF SECTION 1.24.010 OF THIS CODE.
F.
THE OBSTRUCTION OF ANY STREET, ALLEY, OR DRIVEWAY WITHIN A
PUBLIC RIGHT-OF-WAY BY THE STORAGE OR PLACEMENT OF MATERIALS,
EQUIPMENT OR OTHER TANGIBLE PERSONAL PROPERTY THEREIN IN ANY MANNER
WHICH VIOLATES THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF A RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE
PERMIT ISSUED BY THE CITY ENGINEER IN ACCORDANCE WITH CHAPTER 12.04 OF
THIS CODE SHALL CONSTITUTE A NUISANCE AND A MISDEMEANOR PUNISHABLE
IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE PENALTY PROVISIONS OF SECTION 1.24.010 OF THIS
CODE.
G.
THE PERFORMANCE OF ANY CONSTRUCTION, EXCAVATION, OR OTHER
WORK WITHIN OR UPON ANY SIDEWALK, CURB AND GUTTER, DRIVEWAY,
ROADWAY OR STREET WITHOUT HAVING OBTAINED A RIGHT-OF-WAY
ENCROACHMENT PERMIT FROM THE CITY ENGINEER, OR FOLLOWING THE
EXPIRATION OF A SUCH A PERMIT, SHALL CONSTITUTE A NUISANCE AND A
MISDEMEANOR PUNISHABLE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE PENALTY PROVISIONS OF
SECTION 1.24.010 OF THIS CODE.
H.
THE PERFORMANCE OF ANY CONSTRUCTION, EXCAVATION, OR OTHER
WORK WITHIN OR UPON ANY SIDEWALK, CURB AND GUTTER, DRIVEWAY,
ROADWAY OR STREET IN ANY MANNER WHICH VIOLATES THE TERMS AND
CONDITIONS OF A RIGHT-OF-WAY ENCROACHMENT PERMIT ISSUED BY THE CITY
ENGINEER IN ACCORDANCE WITH CHAPTER 12.04 OF THIS CODE SHALL CONSTITUTE
A NUISANCE AND A MISDEMEANOR PUNISHABLE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE
PENALTY PROVISIONS OF SECTION 1.24.010 OF THIS CODE.
I.
FOR THE PURPOSES OF THIS CHAPTER, THE PHRASE “MATERIALS,
EQUIPMENT OR OTHER TANGIBLE PERSONAL PROPERTY” SHALL NOT INCLUDE ANY
“MOTOR VEHICLE” OR “VEHICLE” AS DEFINED IN WYO. STAT. SECTION 31-1-101(A);
NOR SHALL THE PHRASE INCLUDE REFUSE CONTAINERS SMALLER THAN TWO (2)
CUBIC YARDS IN SIZE PLACED IN ACCORDANCE WITH CHAPTER 8.44 OF THIS CODE.
Section
2.

That
Section
12.04.080,
Construction
and
repair–Permits
required–Fees–Exception, of Chapter 12.04, Streets, Sidewalks and Driveways Generally, of Title
12, Streets, Sidewalks and Public Places, of the Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, is
amended as follows:
12.04.080
Construction, and repair, AND STORAGE IN RIGHT-OF-WAY–Permits
required– Fees–Exception.
A.
RIGHT-OF-WAY ENCROACHMENT PERMIT.  No person may construct, remove
or repair any sidewalk, curb and gutter, driveway, roadway or street, or perform any EXCAVATION
OR other work within the public right-of-way without first obtaining a right-of-way encroachment
permit.  Right-of-way encroachment permit and plan review fees for work in the public right-of-way
shall be based on the valuation of the work and paid in accordance with the schedule of permit fees
contained in Section 15.08.030.  If the work to be done in the right-of-way is in conjunction with
a building permit, a separate right-of-way encroachment permit is required.
B.
Exception. None, unless waived specifically by the city engineer.
