### Page 3 of 4

```text
3
B.
RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE PERMIT.  SUBJECT TO THE TERMS AND
CONDITIONS THIS SECTION, THE CITY ENGINEER MAY ISSUE A RIGHT-OF-WAY
STORAGE PERMIT FOR THE STORAGE OR PLACEMENT OF MATERIALS, EQUIPMENT
OR OTHER TANGIBLE PERSONAL PROPERTY IN THE RIGHT-OF-WAY SUBJECT TO
SUCH TERMS AND CONDITIONS AS THE CITY ENGINEER MAY DETERMINE TO BE
NECESSARY FOR THE PROTECTION OF THE PUBLIC HEALTH AND SAFETY.  AN
APPLICANT FOR A RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE PERMIT SHALL COMPLETE AN
APPLICATION FORM PRESCRIBED BY THE CITY ENGINEER.
C.
FOR RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE IN COMMERCIAL, MIXED USE, AND
INDUSTRIAL DISTRICTS, AS DEFINED IN ARTICLE 5 OF THE UNIFIED DEVELOPMENT
CODE (“UDC”), THE CITY ENGINEER SHALL CHARGE A FEE FOR THE ISSUANCE OF A
RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE PERMIT IN THE AMOUNT OF FIVE DOLLARS ($5.00) PER
DAY, OR PART OF A DAY, ISSUE A RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE PERMIT AT NO COST TO
THE APPLICANT, THAT THE PERMIT WILL BE IN EFFECT, BEGINNING WITH THE DATE
OF ISSUANCE AND CONTINUING THROUGH THE DATE OF TERMINATION STATED IN
THE PERMIT.
D.
FOR
RIGHT-OF-WAY
STORAGE
IN
RURAL,
AGRICULTURAL,
RESIDENTIAL NEIGHBORHOOD, SPECIAL PURPOSE AND OVERLAY DISTRICTS, AS
DEFINED IN ARTICLE 5 OF THE UNIFIED DEVELOPMENT CODE (“UDC”), THE CITY
ENGINEER SHALL CHARGE A FEE FOR THE ISSUANCE OF A RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE
PERMIT IN THE AMOUNT OF FIVE DOLLARS ($5.00) PER DAY, OR PART OF A DAY,
THAT THE PERMIT WILL BE IN EFFECT UP TO A MAXIMUM OF FIFTEEN (15) DAYS.
IF THE APPLICANT DESIRES THAT THE PERMIT REMAIN IN EFFECT FOR MORE THAN
FIFTEEN (15) DAYS, THE CITY ENGINEER SHALL CHARGE A PERMIT FEE OF TEN
DOLLARS ($10.00) PER DAY, OR PART OF A DAY, UP TO A MAXIMUM OF FIFTEEN (15)
ADDITIONAL DAYS.  ISSUE A RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE PERMIT AT NO CHARGE TO
THE APPLICANT.  THE PERMIT WILL BE IN EFFECT UP TO A MAXIMUM OF SEVEN (7)
DAYS.
E.
THE CITY ENGINEER SHALL NOT ISSUE A RIGHT-OF-WAY STORAGE
PERMIT FOR STORAGE IN RURAL, AGRICULTURAL, RESIDENTIAL NEIGHBORHOOD,
SPECIAL PURPOSE OR OVERLAY DISTRICTS, FOR A PERIOD OF TIME LONGER THAN
THIRTY (30) CONSECUTIVE DAYS.
F. E.
EACH PERMIT ISSUED PURSUANT TO THIS SECTION SHALL BE
CONSPICUOUSLY POSTED AT THE SITE DESIGNATED IN THE PERMIT DURING THE
ENTIRE PERIOD THAT SAID PERMIT IS EFFECTIVE.
G. F.
PERSONS ENGAGED IN THE BUSINESS OF RENTING STORAGE
CONTAINERS OR REFUSE CONTAINERS (“ROLL-OFF CONTAINERS”) WITH CAPACITIES
OF TWO (2) CUBIC YARDS OR GREATER SHALL ADD REFLECTIVE TAPE, AND SUCH
OTHER WARNING OR TRAFFIC CONTROL MEASURES AS MAY BE REQUIRED BY THE
CITY ENGINEER, TO EACH SUCH CONTAINER AND SHALL ALSO NOTIFY THEIR
CUSTOMERS OF THE REQUIREMENTS OF THIS CHAPTER.
```

